# Implementing `useExplicitLengthCheck` in Biome — Investigation Report

Note: the repo root is `/workspace/repo` (not `/workspace/crates/...`). All paths below are absolute.

## Key finding up front: there's a codegen scaffold

Biome generates new rules via `just new-js-lintrule useExplicitLengthCheck` (defined at `/workspace/repo/justfile:59-60`, which runs `cargo run -p xtask_codegen -- new-lintrule --kind=js --name=useExplicitLengthCheck`). The template lives at `/workspace/repo/xtask/codegen/src/generate_new_lintrule.rs` and scaffolds the rule file, the `nursery.rs` registration, the category, and config entries. The registration files (`nursery.rs`, `biome_configuration/src/linter/rules.rs`) are all marked "Generated file, do not edit by hand, see `xtask/codegen`". You typically run codegen (`cargo codegen analyzer` / `cargo codegen configuration`) after writing the rule so these stay in sync. You can still hand-edit if you prefer.

---

## 1. Representative "refactor/fix" nursery rules with a code action

### (a) `NoFlatMapIdentity` — works on member/call expressions, has a `Safe` fix
`/workspace/repo/crates/biome_js_analyze/src/lint/nursery/no_flat_map_identity.rs`

Imports and rule shape (lines 1-52):
```rust
